From 57db633c4fede72f7aa001b7dedcdc67bf7e614e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 1 May 2017 19:18:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH]     CSettings: Narrow the patch: restore the
 CSettings::Save() in CApplication::Stop(),     keep the uptime store and the
 skin-settings save removed.

    Without it, nothing saves guisettings.xml on any exit path, and once Stop()
    sets m_bStop, CApplication::OnSettingsSaving() vetoes every later save. State
    that is only ever written as a side effect of some other Save() - volume and
    mute, JSON-RPC Settings.SetSettingValue, the walkthrough's setters, settings
    pages left without Back - is lost on reboot unless something else happened to
    save first. That is the reported "change something else and everything gets
    written out" behaviour.

    The 2017 reasons for removing the save no longer hold: SIGTERM is now graceful
    (upstream RequestQuit -> TMSG_QUIT -> Stop()), and Stop() runs before
    Powerdown()/Reboot() since the Nexus rebase, so the save cannot be killed
    mid-write by the OS shutdown.

    Uptime stays out so that 'Save settings only if they were modified after the
    last save' skips the write when nothing changed. The skin save stays out
    because skin settings are saved on change and again in UnloadSkin().

    See docs/osmc/settings-persistence.md.

Signed-off-by: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
---
 xbmc/application/Application.cpp | 25 +++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/application/Application.cpp b/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
index 365210c69d..607168b6e6 100644
--- a/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
@@ -2153,24 +2153,13 @@ bool CApplication::Stop(int exitCode)
 
     g_alarmClock.StopThread();
 
-    CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Storing total System Uptime");
-    g_sysinfo.SetTotalUptime(g_sysinfo.GetTotalUptime() + (int)(CTimeUtils::GetFrameTime() / 60000));
-
-    // Update the settings information (volume, uptime etc. need saving)
-    if (CFile::Exists(CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetProfileManager()->GetSettingsFile()))
-    {
-      CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Saving settings");
-      CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetSettings()->Save();
-    }
-    else
-      CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Not saving settings (settings.xml is not present)");
-
-    // kodi may crash or deadlock during exit (shutdown / reboot) due to
-    // either a bug in core or misbehaving addons. so try saving
-    // skin settings early
-    CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Saving skin settings");
-    if (g_SkinInfo != nullptr)
-      g_SkinInfo->SaveSettings();
+    // Flush in-memory state that nothing else saves (volume, JSON-RPC changes, ...).
+    // Must run before m_bStop is set: from then on OnSettingsSaving() vetoes every save.
+    // Uptime is deliberately not stored, so the unchanged-file check in CSettings::Save()
+    // can skip the write when nothing changed.
+    const auto settingsComponent = CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent();
+    if (CFile::Exists(settingsComponent->GetProfileManager()->GetSettingsFile()))
+      settingsComponent->GetSettings()->Save();
 
     m_bStop = true;
     // Add this here to keep the same ordering behaviour for now
-- 
